# AV Asset Manager

- Stack: Laravel + Blade + Alpine + Tailwind + Sanctum + Spatie Permission + MariaDB (SQLite OK locally).
- TP brand colours via Tailwind `brand-*` tokens (`#00adb7`, black, white, charcoal). Minimal UI; mobile-first.
- Roles are permission sets: `admin` (full operational access; developer features stay on the profile), `inventory_manager`, `scanner`, `external_repairer`, plus custom roles. New routes use permission middleware. `external_repairer` is limited to Maintenance/Repairs assigned to them (and related asset show); keep them out of the broad staff route group.
- Audit logs are immutable — never add update/delete endpoints or Eloquent updates for `AuditLog`. Asset History is a read-only UI over `audit_logs`.
- Per-user preferences live in `users.preferences`: `asset_table_columns` (Assets index / list browse) and `dashboard_modules` (enable/disable/reorder dashboard widgets).
- Admin settings / sub-pages (`/admin/*`, e.g. users, roles, departments, export columns, storage, SSO, email settings) belong in the profile dropdown (and matching mobile Account/Admin section)—not as top-level nav links. Operational items (Import, Data, Reports, Maintenance) stay in the main nav.
- Online-only PWA. Do **not** add offline IndexedDB / queued scan sync unless explicitly requested. Guest QR stock tokens, RU visualiser, maintenance files, manuals, SSO, checkout (`AssetCheckoutService`), repairs/spares, unknown-scan link, and email digests already exist — extend only when asked.
- Prefer services (`ScanService`, `ListComparisonService`, `AssetCheckoutService`) for stocktake/checkout logic. Keep controllers thin.
- No secrets in commits. Validate uploads (xlsx/csv/jpg/png/pdf/docx, 25MB).
- Follow existing naming: Asset, AssetList, ScanSession, custom field sets on ItemType, AssetCheckout, Repair, SparePart.
- MySQL/MariaDB identifiers max 64 chars — for long table/column pairs, give FKs/indexes explicit short names (see `.cursor/rules/mysql-identifier-length.mdc`).
